From 68d40d27a9b5099f31a5d7e87b704eb3d7995606 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 10:23:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 42/55] Drone: one tone rendered on its own, for drone tracks;
 tone attributes and the block's context shared

Groundwork for drone tracks (kits of drone rows, next commits), without changing the song's drone:

- Drone::renderTone() renders one tone with a Voice of the caller's (Drone::Voice is public now), through the
  existing renderVoice() and renderLivelyVoice() (a Pulse tone, at the drone's default width), as render() does for a
  tone of the drone, with a gain in place of the drone's volume and without life and FM. Both functions are
  untouched: their machine code is the same as v15's (renderVoice() and render() instruction for instruction,
  renderLivelyVoice() apart from the addresses of static data), and the song test's measured.wav is still v14's
  (87a7df29, EMU_OPTS="--init-sounds --seed 1"). tests/drone: renderTone() is render()'s tone bit for bit in every
  mode, a Pulse, glides, mode changes and off/on, in blocks of 128 and 37.
- DroneTrackPitch: a drone row's pitch, its tone's own with an Hz lane on top in cents (2^31 is +9600 cents, as MIDI
  pitch bend reaches 8 octaves; 0 changes nothing), what renderTone() gets for a gate and a lane value (the frequency
  to a hundredth of a hertz once the lane has moved it), and the lane's value for a frequency or a step in cents.
- Tone::writeAttributes()/readAttribute(): the tone's attributes in a file, shared by the song's drone and drone
  rows. The song's drone writes them in the same order as before, so its XML is unchanged.
- AudioEngine::getDroneContext(): tempo, song position and master tune for the block, taken out of renderDrone() so
  drone rows render by the same clock (synced beats lock to the grid).

